# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""V05: ornamented red wall scabbard for one knife, standard FreeCAD 1.1.3 objects only.

Model frame = installed frame = print frame (nothing is rotated for export):
  Z up, closed end on the bed at Z = 0, mouth at Parameters.MouthZ;
  X along the wall (the 45 mm blade height), blade centred on X = 0;
  Y depth: blade plane at Y = 0, the room towards -Y, the flat wall plane at Y = +BladeAxisFromWall.

All solids are one PartDesign::Body. Sketches are fully constrained and driven by the Parameters
sheet. No Python proxy, no element references (chamfers come from 45 degree tapered pads), so the
saved document recomputes without this macro.

Overwrites ONLY its own FCStd, STL and JSON beside this macro. Earlier revisions and the printer
are never read or modified. Reference knife objects are illustrations, not measurements.
"""
